@* AppQuestionCard.razor — shared reusable question-bank list item (CLAUDE.md
   §3.1), Screen B's "مجمع بنوك العناصر" column. Read directly off
   demo/ScreenB/UI_ UX 2.jpeg (the only reference that actually shows this
   list — TaskTwo_from_figma_design.png and its Tablet/Mobile companions all
   cut off just above it), CLAUDE.md rule 1.

   ANATOMY CONFIRMED PER CARD (3 sample cards zoomed/cropped individually):
     - A primary tag (solid blue pill: "AudioTest" / a long ID string /
       "سؤال-2") + a secondary tag (solid dark pill: "بنك اسئلة") stacked
       VERTICALLY, at the card's own left edge.
     - Question text (when present — one of the 3 sample cards has none at
       all, just its two tags), multi-line, filling the space between the
       tags and the icons.
     - A small help icon (Icons.Material.Filled.Quiz — a document+"?" glyph,
       closest standard match to the reference's icon) + an unchecked
       checkbox, both at the card's right edge, checkbox rightmost.

   DRAG HANDLE — FLAGGED, NOT CONFIRMED: no drag-handle glyph is clearly
   visible on any of the 3 sample cards at this JPEG's resolution (checked
   both tight per-icon crops and full-card-width crops). Included anyway
   per instruction (this component's whole purpose is an upcoming
   drag-and-drop pass) using the same DragIndicator icon already
   established for drag affordance elsewhere in this library (AppToggleGroup
   "سحب وإملاء"), placed at the row's own outer/right edge — an ASSUMED
   position, not read off the image. Flag if it shouldn't be there, or
   belongs on the opposite edge.

   TAGS — NOT AppChip: AppChip is a single-color light-tint pill with an
   optional icon (Screen B's "نموذج 1" tag). These are a different, simpler
   pattern — solid-fill, no icon, two color variants (checked against
   tokens.css/components.css first, per instruction) — so they render as
   plain .app-tag spans (components.css) instead, not a second Blazor
   component: "simple enough it doesn't need its own states" applies here
   even more than it did to AppChip itself.

   CHECKBOX — plain native <input type="checkbox"> (CLAUDE.md §6: native
   semantic HTML first), wrapped in a <label> padded to the
   --a11y-touch-target-min hit area (44×44) even though the visible box
   stays small — clicking anywhere in the label toggles the input natively,
   no JS needed. No visible text label exists for it in the reference, so
   its accessible name is synthesized from PrimaryTagLabel/Text.

   Help icon and drag handle are both decorative only this pass (no
   real tooltip/drag behavior yet, per instruction) — aria-hidden, no
   focus stop, no cursor affordance implying working drag. *@
<div class="app-question-card">
    <MudIcon Icon="@Icons.Material.Filled.DragIndicator" Color="Color.Inherit" Class="app-question-card__drag-handle" aria-hidden="true" />

    <label class="app-question-card__select">
        <input type="checkbox"
               class="app-question-card__checkbox"
               checked="@Checked"
               @onchange="OnCheckedChangedAsync"
               aria-label="@($"تحديد {Text ?? PrimaryTagLabel}")" />
    </label>

    <MudIcon Icon="@Icons.Material.Filled.Quiz" Color="Color.Inherit" Class="app-question-card__help-icon" aria-hidden="true" />

    @if (!string.IsNullOrWhiteSpace(Text))
    {
        <p class="app-question-card__text">@Text</p>
    }

    <div class="app-question-card__tags">
        <span class="app-tag app-tag--primary">@PrimaryTagLabel</span>
        @if (!string.IsNullOrWhiteSpace(SecondaryTagLabel))
        {
            <span class="app-tag app-tag--neutral">@SecondaryTagLabel</span>
        }
    </div>
</div>

@code {
    [Parameter, EditorRequired] public string PrimaryTagLabel { get; set; } = string.Empty;

    /// Second, dark pill (e.g. "بنك اسئلة") — optional since it's plausible
    /// a future card only needs one tag; every sample in the reference
    /// happens to show both.
    [Parameter] public string? SecondaryTagLabel { get; set; }

    /// Question text — null renders no <p> at all (one of the 3 reference
    /// cards has no question text, just its two tags), not an empty one.
    [Parameter] public string? Text { get; set; }

    [Parameter] public bool Checked { get; set; }
    [Parameter] public EventCallback<bool> CheckedChanged { get; set; }

    private Task OnCheckedChangedAsync(ChangeEventArgs e)
    {
        var isChecked = e.Value is bool value && value;
        return CheckedChanged.HasDelegate ? CheckedChanged.InvokeAsync(isChecked) : Task.CompletedTask;
    }
}
